 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "동물에 관한 표현 (have, can)",
   "en": "Talking about animals (have, can)"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "반려동물이 있다고 말할 때는 have를 씁니다: I have a dog. 동물의 특징은 be + 형용사나 can + 동사로 말합니다: The dog is big. The dog can run fast. 동물 이름의 소유는 's로 표현합니다: the dog's name.",
   "en": "Say you have a pet with have: I have a dog. Describe animals with be + adjective or can + verb: The dog is big. The dog can run fast. Use 's for ownership: the dog's name."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "have + 동물",
     "I have a dog."
    ],
    [
     "be + 형용사",
     "The dog is big."
    ],
    [
     "can + 동사",
     "The dog can run fast."
    ],
    [
     "'s",
     "the dog's name"
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "fish는 단수와 복수가 같습니다.",
    "en": "Fish is the same in singular and plural."
   },
   {
    "ko": "he / she / it에는 has: She has a cat.",
    "en": "With she use has: She has a cat."
   },
   {
    "ko": "동물은 보통 it, 이름이 있는 반려동물은 he / she로도 말해요.",
    "en": "Animals are usually it, but pets with names can be he / she."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
